{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772651018,"nonce":"Ev0G/rSAOugDwmsiEuPe9yXgH1c=","title":"mandible auth request: background task exits with non-zero code on success","message":"When `mandible auth request` runs as a background task (via run_in_background), it exits with code 23 after the auth succeeds. The SSE listener correctly detects completion (logs \"completed (exit 0)\") but the shell process itself exits non-zero, causing Claude Code to report the task as \"failed\".\n\nShould exit 0 when the auth request completes successfully. The non-zero exit is likely from the SSE curl connection dropping after the event is received, or from cleanup code after the listener loop.\n\nAlso observed: `mandible auth request` printed \"Mandible unreachable. Falling back to terminal pane...\" even though Mandible was fully running and responding to API calls.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue 2fa626e.","files":null}]}